Looking at the cuboid (5×2×2), the white piece shows three cubes along the top back row. The only hidden positions are the bottom back row, and connectivity forces the white piece to include the two bottom cubes beneath the middle of that row (the light gray piece must take the back-bottom left cube, and the dark gray piece must take the back-bottom right cube to stay connected).

So the white piece is a 2×2 block of cubes with one extra cube attached on top of one end — a flat "P" shape. Checking the options (rotations allowed): this matches diagram E (a 2×2 block with one cube on top), after a 180° rotation about a vertical axis.

